  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A spherical body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> starting from rest acquires a kinetic energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> at the end of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>5</mn><mtext>th&#160;</mtext></msup></math> second. The force acted on the body is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "40",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given kinetic energy,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Also,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>at</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Therefore, force acting</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>"
  }
